findings.recommendation:
Register both teardown steps through t.Cleanup so LIFO ordering puts the DROP before the Close, and surface the error instead of discarding it:
```go
admin, err := sql.Open("mysql", adminDSN)
if err != nil { t.Fatalf(...) }
t.Cleanup(func() { _ = admin.Close() })          // registered first -> runs last
...
t.Cleanup(func() {                                // registered second -> runs first
    if _, err := admin.Exec("DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS " + dbName); err != nil {
        t.Errorf("drop throwaway database %s: %v", dbName, err)
    }
})
```
Same treatment for `defer db.Close()` on line 72 (it must also close before the DROP, so it can stay a defer, but converting both to t.Cleanup keeps the ordering rule in one place). Then drop the five already-leaked databases by hand.
